senses.gloss:
सारण, अस्, ई, अम्, (fr. Caus. of rt. सृ), caus-
ing to go or flow; (अस्), m. dysentery, diarrhœa
[cf. अति-सार]; the hog-plum, Spondias Mangifera;
another plant (= भद्र-बला); N. of one of Rā-
vaṇa's ministers (sent as ambassador to Rāma);
(अम्), n. a kind of perfume.

सरणि, इस्, f. a road, path, way [cf. 2. शरणि];
a straight or continuous line; the creeping plant
Pæderia Fetida; a disease of the throat.

सारणि, इस्, f. a canal, drain, channel, water-pipe;
a small river; the plant Pæderia Fetida; [cf. सा-
रणी.]

शर्मर, अस्, m. a sort of garment or cloth;
(आ), f. a kind of Curcuma, Curcuma Xanthorrhiza
(= दारु-हरिद्रा).

शार् शार् (also written सार्), cl. 10. P.
शारयति, -यितुम्, to be weak or feeble;
to weaken; [cf. rt. शॄ.]

सरङ्ग स-रङ्ग, अस्, आ, अम्, having colour;
having a nasal sound; (अस्), m. a quadruped; a bird;
[cf. सारङ्ग.]

शार्ङ्गरव शार्ङ्गरव, अस्, m. (fr. शृङ्ग-
रव?), a Śārṅgarava man, see Pāṇ. IV. 1, 73;
(ई), f. a Śāṅgarava woman.

सर्पण, अम्, n. the act of creeping or gliding;
going tortuously; the flight of an arrow nearly
parallel with the ground.

सार्वभौतिक, अस्, ई, अम् (fr. सर्व-भूत),
belonging or relating to all elements or beings, &c.;
comprising all animated beings.
